---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { retractions, standingClaims } from '../data/retractions';
---

<Base
  title="Retractions — fibtransponder"
  description="Six claims this repository made and withdrew, with the measurement that withdrew each one, and what replaced them."
  kicker="Audit"
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>What this project got wrong</h1>
    <p class="lede measure">
      A research repository that only publishes its successes is a marketing document. These are
      the claims <strong>fibtransponder</strong> made and then removed from the record, each with
      the measurement that did it and the position that replaced it.
    </p>
    <p class="measure">
      Two of these were found by writing the test that was supposed to exist. Two were found by
      the arithmetic of the thing itself. One was found by noticing that a benchmark table had
      mixed hardware. One was a classifier measuring itself on its own tuning data.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="chevron"><span>Withdrawn</span></div>

  <ol class="log">
    {
      retractions.map((r, i) => (
        <li class="entry panel">
          <p class="entry__no num" aria-hidden="true">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</p>
          <div class="entry__body">
            <p class="label">
              <span class="tag tag-retract">Retracted</span>
              {r.pinnedAt && <code class="entry__pin">{r.pinnedAt}</code>}
            </p>
            <h2 class="entry__claim">“{r.claim}”</h2>
            <p class="entry__ev"><strong>Evidence.</strong> {r.evidence}</p>
            <p class="entry__why"><strong>Why it was withdrawn.</strong> {r.withdrawnBecause}</p>
            <p class="entry__now verified-note note">
              <strong>Now claimed.</strong> {r.nowClaim}
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <div class="chevron"><span>Still standing</span></div>

  <section aria-labelledby="standing">
    <h2 id="standing" class="measure">What the project still claims</h2>
    <p class="measure">
      A retraction log is only useful next to the claims that survived it.
    </p>

    <ul class="standing">
      {
        standingClaims.map((c) => (
          <li class="panel">
            <h3>{c.claim}</h3>
            <p>{c.basis}</p>
            <code class="standing__pin">{c.pinnedAt}</code>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="principle panel framed measure">
    <h2>The rule this repository follows</h2>
    <p>
      A comment saying <em>“do not do the wrong thing”</em> did not stop the wrong thing happening
      twice. An <strong>assertion</strong> did. Every retraction above is now backed by a test that
      fails if the retracted claim starts looking true again — which is how the sketch fold bug
      survived in two files for as long as it did, and why the regression tests here
      <a href="https://github.com/shaoyanji/fibtransponder/blob/master/internal/transponder/sketch_fold_test.go">check both call sites independently</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The same rule applies to this site: the interactive demos call the repository's own Go,
      compiled to WebAssembly. A number cannot go stale here, because there is nothing to store it.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page-head {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .page-head h1 {
    margin-bottom: 1.1rem;
  }
  .page-head p + p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
  }

  .log {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .entry {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.6rem 1.75rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--retract);
  }

  .entry__no {
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--retract);
    /* No opacity here. It looks like a softer accent but it compounds with the
       colour: 0.55 alpha over the light surface lands at 2.49:1, below the
       3:1 large-text floor. Colour alone gets 5.64:1. */
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .entry__claim {
    font-size: 1.18rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 0.65rem 0 1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .entry__ev,
  .entry__why {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }

  .entry__now {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .entry__pin {
    font-size: 0.66rem;
    color: var(--ink-mute);
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .standing {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.15rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 19rem), 1fr));
  }

  .standing li {
    padding: 1.3rem 1.4rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--verify);
  }

  .standing h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.38;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .standing p {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    line-height: 1.55;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
  }

  .standing__pin {
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    color: var(--verify);
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .principle {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding: 1.75rem 1.9rem;
  }
  .principle h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
  }
  .principle p {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .principle p + p {
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .entry {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    .entry__no {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
